{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 45, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the distant shore of Japan doth thou desire to set foot? Fear not, for I shall provide an itinerary, crafted in the style of the noble Shakespeare, to guide thee on thy journey.\n\nMethinks our tale shall begin in the ancient city of Kyoto, where the Imperial Palace doth stand. Marvel at its beauty and grandeur, and pay homage to the Emperor's former residence.\n\nNext, journey to the Golden Pavilion, Kinkaku-ji, a sight to behold with its golden facade mirrored upon the surface of the nearby pond. Let not its tranquility fool thee, for this structure hides a tumultuous past.\n \\*\nThen, make thy way to Arashiyama, where the Bamboo Grove awaits. Meander through the towering stalks, and let the wind whisper secrets in thy ear.\n\nIn the land of the rising sun, thou must witness its first light. Therefore, set thy course for Fushimi Inari Taisha, where thou shalt find a thousand torii gates leading to the peak of the mountain. Begin thy ascent at dawn, and reach the summit as the sun doth rise.\n\nHark! The sound of water doth beckon thee to the Katsura Rikyu Imperial Villa. Observe its exquisite gardens, and ponder the fleeting nature of life as thou gazest upon the carp swimming in the pond.\n\nThy journey would be incomplete without a visit to Nara. Feed the sacred deer that roam the park, and marvel at the Great Buddha of Todai-ji.\n\nLastly, indulge in the pleasures of the modern world in Tokyo. Wander through the bustling streets of Shibuya, and let the neon lights dazzle thee. Visit the Meiji Shrine, where the souls of the Emperor and Empress Meiji rest.\n\nAnd so, with this itinerary, thy journey through Japan is complete. May it bring thee joy and adventure, and mayst thou return home with memories to last a lifetime.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.16018113493919373}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0139404647052